# Defaults for an interactive Anaconda run.
#
# Anaconda reads this only when the kernel command line carries no inst.ks=.
# It is a kickstart, but without the automated flags, so the installer still
# stops and asks for anything left unconfigured -- the disk, in our case.
#
# @PAYLOAD_SRC@ / @PAYLOAD_TARGET@ are substituted by Containerfile.installer:
#
#   source -- what bootc copies from. A name in the installer's own container
#             storage, so it needs the containers-storage: transport and must
#             match --bootc-installer-payload-ref exactly.
#   target -- what the installed system tracks for updates. A registry
#             reference; pykickstart rejects a transport prefix here.
#
# `xconfig --startxonboot` pins graphical.target. Left alone, Anaconda only
# picks graphical when it can prove the target has a graphical login manager
# and falls back to multi-user.target otherwise, i.e. a console-only system.
#
# `bootloader --append` is the only reliable way to get kernel arguments onto
# the installed system with a bootc payload. Anaconda assembles them in
# collect_arguments() from five sources, and the one that looks obvious -- its
# rhgb/quiet heuristic -- never fires here: it asks the *target's* rpm database
# whether plymouth is installed, and Anaconda collects the arguments before
# bootc has deployed anything, so the database is empty. bootloader --append is
# the unconditional source, and Anaconda turns its contents into
# `bootc install --karg=` arguments. Without rhgb, plymouthd runs in text mode
# and the boot ends up as scrolling text instead of the splash.
#
# Do not add --location=none to "avoid touching the bootloader": it switches the
# bootloader mode to SKIPPED, and CollectKernelArgumentsTask returns before
# collecting anything, so these arguments would be dropped along with it.
#
# No storage directives on purpose: that is what makes Anaconda show the
# Installation Destination page and let the user pick the disk.
bootc --source-imgref containers-storage:@PAYLOAD_SRC@ --target-imgref @PAYLOAD_TARGET@

bootloader --append="rhgb quiet"

xconfig --startxonboot
